  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/26-flatfishes/catathyridium-jenynsii-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species attains a maximum length of about 20-25 cm; thus it is a rather large fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/26-flatfishes/catathyridium-jenynsii-2/",
      "html": "<p>This is a southern species, so the water temperature should be lowered from time to time. Given the tank is placed in a living room it is best to switch off the aquarium heater during the winter.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/26-flatfishes/catathyridium-jenynsii-2/",
      "html": "<p>The bottom in a flatfish tank must contain places with fine sand where the fish can bury themselves, otherwise they will get skin diseases.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/26-flatfishes/catathyridium-jenynsii-2/",
      "html": "<p>Besides fish and chopped fish pieces, the flatfish will readily accept earthworms.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/26-flatfishes/catathyridium-jenynsii-2/",
      "html": "<p>As Catathyridium jenynsii are predatory fish one should not choose too small other fish as tankmates, for they might be eaten. Against other fish Catathyridium jenynsii is absolutely peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/26-flatfishes/catathyridium-jenynsii-2/",
      "html": "<p>Kai Arendt suggested a common name for the fish: Bearded Paraná Sole, due to the great number of cirrhi around the head.</p>"
    }
  ],
